# Testing Conventions

## Framework

- Use Node's built-in test runner: `node:test` + `node:assert/strict`
- Do **not** add Jest, Vitest, Mocha, or React Testing Library
- Live / API checks are plain `scripts/*.mjs` (custom assert or ✔/✖), not `node:test`
- Browser UI E2E uses **Puppeteer** (already a dependency). Prefer extending it over adding Playwright unless Puppeteer cannot cover the case
- Never call real BusyBee SendSMS in default CI/unit runs. Live DLR requires `SEND_LIVE_SMS=1`

## Structure

- Unit / seam: `tests/<name>.test.js` — one concern per file
- Live e2e: `scripts/e2e-*.mjs`, `scripts/check-*.mjs`, `scripts/smoke-*.mjs`, `scripts/qa-*.mjs`
- Evidence: `e2e-evidence/` for UI/responsive screenshots
- Bug register: `docs/qa/BUGS.md`

## Patterns

- Prefer pure helpers over mocking internals
- When HTTP is needed in-unit, use local fakes (see `tests/httpCors.test.js`)
- Static source contracts use `readFileSync` + `assert.match` (see `tests/frontendAudit.test.js`)
- Ops UI auth false-green: reject `/operations/login` via `scripts/screenshotAuth.mjs`

## Examples to follow

- `tests/queueLogic.test.js` — pure domain unit
- `tests/httpCors.test.js` — in-process mock response
- `tests/principalQaMatrix.test.js` — RBAC lock
- `tests/screenshotAuth.test.js` — auth URL guard
- `scripts/e2e-readiness.mjs` — live Supabase smoke style
- `scripts/e2e-ui-p0.mjs` — Puppeteer P0 flows

## Commands

- `npm test` — all `tests/` via `node --test`
- `npm run test:readiness` — ultimate orchestrator (unit + live slices + UI + responsive)
- `npm run e2e:newrequest` — Parts 1–9 master suite
